      nursingEssentials: ["Assess airway, breathing, oxygenation, pulse, pressure, mental status, chest discomfort, heart failure, rhythm strip, 12-lead ECG, IV access, and reversible causes in parallel.", "During pacing, confirm both electrical capture and a corresponding pulse or arterial waveform; provide analgesia or sedation when hemodynamics permit without sacrificing perfusion."],
      interactions: ["Beta blockers, non-dihydropyridine calcium-channel blockers, digoxin, antiarrhythmics, sedatives, and cholinergic exposures can contribute to bradycardia and alter response.", "Epinephrine or dopamine with other sympathomimetics raises tachyarrhythmia and ischemia risk, but emergency benefit may still dominate under continuous monitoring."],
