      contraindications: ["A prior immediate anaphylactic or severe delayed beta-lactam reaction requires precise phenotype review and agent-specific risk assessment rather than a vague allergy checkbox.", "Do not choose by generation alone. Confirm organism, site, local susceptibility, renal function, CNS penetration need, Pseudomonas or MRSA requirement, and source control."],
      nursingEssentials: ["Say each drug's defining identity before giving it: cefazolin MSSA/surgery, cephalexin oral skin/strep, cefuroxime respiratory oral prodrug, ceftriaxone long-acting with neonatal cautions, ceftazidime Pseudomonas, cefepime broad Pseudomonas with neurotoxicity, ceftaroline MRSA without Pseudomonas.", "Trend response and culture data, then de-escalate. Broad empiric coverage is a temporary hypothesis, not proof that the chosen drug matches the organism."],
