      keyLabs: ["Glucose, CBC and platelets, PT/INR, aPTT, renal function, pregnancy testing when relevant, type and screen when indicated, and protocol-specific brain or vascular imaging.", "Trend neurologic status, blood pressure, airway, puncture sites, urine/stool/emesis, hemoglobin, and follow-up imaging rather than relying on the infusion ending safely."],
      nclexTraps: ["Alteplase converts plasminogen to plasmin; it is not an antiplatelet, an anticoagulant, or a mechanical thrombectomy device.", "Do not reflexively give aspirin immediately after stroke alteplase. Follow protocol after hemorrhage reassessment and post-treatment imaging."],
      populationRisks: populationRisks("Systemic pediatric thrombolysis is specialist-directed because evidence, dosing, and hemorrhage risk differ by indication; Cathflo catheter use has its own product rules.", "Advanced age increases hemorrhage risk but is not interpreted in isolation; baseline function, severity, imaging, pressure, and comorbidity determine benefit-risk.", "Pregnancy is a high-stakes individualized decision because alteplase does not readily cross the placenta but maternal hemorrhage can be catastrophic; lactation guidance is product and context specific."),
